window.REV_FLIP=window.REV_FLIP||{};window.REV_FLIP["boto3"]=[{"id":"boto3-f0001","card":"q-boto3-001-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"What is boto3 and how does it talk to AWS?","a":"<p>The official AWS SDK for Python. It gives a Pythonic interface to AWS APIs (EC2, S3, Lambda and more). It sends HTTP requests signed with your credentials, and <code>botocore</code> does the low-level work.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0002","card":"q-boto3-001-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"<code>boto3.client</code> vs <code>boto3.resource</code>","a":"<div class=\"table-wrap\">\n  <table>\n    <thead><tr><th></th><th><code>client</code></th><th><code>resource</code></th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Level</td><td>Low-level, maps 1:1 to the API; returns raw dicts/JSON</td><td>Higher-level, object-oriented (buckets, instances as Python objects)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Coverage</td><td>All API operations</td><td>Simpler, but not every service or operation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Use when</td><td>You need precise control or the resource abstraction is missing</td><td>Common tasks, readable code</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\n# Using client\nclient = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\nresponse = client.list_buckets()\nprint(response[&#x27;Buckets&#x27;])\n\n# Using resource\nresource = boto3.resource(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\nfor bucket in resource.buckets.all():\n    print(bucket.name)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0003","card":"q-boto3-001-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"How does boto3 authenticate?","a":"<p>Credential sources, in resolution order:</p>\n<ol>\n  <li>Environment variables (<code>AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID</code>, <code>AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY</code>, <code>AWS_SESSION_TOKEN</code>).</li>\n  <li>Credentials file (<code>~/.aws/credentials</code>).</li>\n  <li>IAM roles for EC2 instances or ECS tasks.</li>\n  <li>AWS CLI SSO or temporary credentials from STS.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>You can also pass credentials explicitly in code or select a named profile (Q19).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0004","card":"q-boto3-001-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"Which services can boto3 manage?","a":"<p>Most of them:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Compute: EC2, Lambda, ECS, EKS</li>\n  <li>Storage: S3, EBS, Glacier</li>\n  <li>Database: DynamoDB, RDS, Redshift</li>\n  <li>Networking: VPC, Route 53, ELB</li>\n  <li>Messaging: SNS, SQS, SES</li>\n  <li>Monitoring: CloudWatch, CloudTrail</li>\n  <li>Management: IAM, CloudFormation, SSM</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0005","card":"q-boto3-001-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"Pagination.","a":"<p>Use paginators. They follow <code>NextToken</code> (or the equivalent marker) automatically.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ns3 = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\npaginator = s3.get_paginator(&#x27;list_objects_v2&#x27;)\nfor page in paginator.paginate(Bucket=&#x27;my-bucket&#x27;):\n    for obj in page.get(&#x27;Contents&#x27;, []):\n        print(obj[&#x27;Key&#x27;])</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0006","card":"q-boto3-002-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"Role of the SDK; how it differs from other AWS SDKs.","a":"<p>boto3 is built on <code>botocore</code> and turns low-level HTTP calls into Python methods. The JavaScript, Java and other SDKs do the same job but differ in syntax, conventions and some features.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0007","card":"q-boto3-002-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"Managing resources programmatically.","a":"<p>Python scripts automate things like creating EC2 instances, uploading to S3 and configuring IAM. It offers both <code>client</code> and <code>resource</code> interfaces and fits scripts, CI/CD pipelines and serverless functions.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0008","card":"q-boto3-002-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"Why boto3 over the Console or CLI?","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Automation: scripted, repeatable tasks.</li>\n  <li>Integration with Python tools and workflows.</li>\n  <li>Scale: manage many resources in code.</li>\n  <li>Flexibility: complex logic and conditionals.</li>\n  <li>Programmatic error handling and retries.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0009","card":"q-boto3-002-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"Integration with DevOps tools","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Kubernetes: manage EKS clusters (node groups) and feed the <code>kubernetes</code> Python client.</li>\n  <li>Terraform: validate or modify Terraform-managed resources.</li>\n  <li>Ansible: generate inventories or pre-provision resources.</li>\n  <li>GitHub Actions: run boto3 scripts in workflows to deploy or manage resources.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0010","card":"q-boto3-002-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"Why IAM roles matter.","a":"<p>Roles give temporary, scoped credentials, so keys are not hardcoded. They enforce least privilege and are the secure choice on EC2, Lambda and CI/CD.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0011","card":"q-boto3-002-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"Error handling.","a":"<p>API errors raise <code>botocore.exceptions.ClientError</code>. Practices: catch specific errors with try/except, use exponential backoff for throttling, log errors, validate inputs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\n\ns3 = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\ntry:\n    s3.head_bucket(Bucket=&#x27;my-bucket&#x27;)\nexcept ClientError as e:\n    print(f&quot;Error: {e.response[&#x27;Error&#x27;][&#x27;Message&#x27;]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0012","card":"q-boto3-002-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"Regions.","a":"<p>Regions are isolated geographic areas. Pass <code>region_name</code> to the client or resource, for example <code>boto3.client('s3', region_name='us-east-1')</code>. If omitted, the default region from AWS configuration is used.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0013","card":"q-boto3-002-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"Limitations","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Needs knowledge of both AWS APIs and Python.</li>\n  <li>API rate limits (throttling).</li>\n  <li>Some services have limited <code>resource</code> support, so you fall back to <code>client</code>.</li>\n  <li>Needs robust exception handling.</li>\n  <li>Steep learning curve versus the Console.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0014","card":"q-boto3-003-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"Serverless (Lambda).","a":"<p>boto3 runs inside Lambda functions to call S3, DynamoDB, SNS and so on. The function's IAM role supplies the credentials. Typical use is event-driven work such as processing S3 uploads or sending notifications.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0015","card":"q-boto3-003-1-core-concepts-q1-15","sec":"boto3-s002","q":"What is <code>botocore</code>?","a":"<p>The low-level library under boto3. It handles HTTP requests, authentication and response parsing. boto3 adds the friendly interface on top.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0016","card":"q-boto3-004-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"List all S3 buckets.","a":"<p>(The source's separate \"Example Artifacts\" script is identical.)</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef list_s3_buckets():\n    s3 = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    response = s3.list_buckets()\n    for bucket in response[&#x27;Buckets&#x27;]:\n        print(f&quot;Bucket: {bucket[&#x27;Name&#x27;]}, Created: {bucket[&#x27;CreationDate&#x27;]}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    list_s3_buckets()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0017","card":"q-boto3-004-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"Create an EC2 instance with specific parameters.","a":"<p>Call <code>run_instances</code> with <code>ImageId</code>, <code>InstanceType</code>, <code>MinCount</code>/<code>MaxCount</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef create_ec2_instance():\n    ec2 = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;)\n    response = ec2.run_instances(\n        ImageId=&#x27;ami-0c55b159cbfafe1f0&#x27;,  # Example AMI ID\n        InstanceType=&#x27;t2.micro&#x27;,\n        MinCount=1,\n        MaxCount=1,\n        KeyName=&#x27;my-key-pair&#x27;,\n        SecurityGroupIds=[&#x27;sg-12345678&#x27;],\n        SubnetId=&#x27;subnet-12345678&#x27;\n    )\n    instance_id = response[&#x27;Instances&#x27;][0][&#x27;InstanceId&#x27;]\n    print(f&quot;Created instance: {instance_id}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    create_ec2_instance()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0018","card":"q-boto3-004-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"Upload a file to S3 and make it public.","a":"<p><code>ExtraArgs={'ACL': 'public-read'}</code>. (Gotcha: this only works if the bucket's Block Public Access and ownership settings allow ACLs.)</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef upload_to_s3(file_path, bucket_name, object_key):\n    s3 = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    s3.upload_file(file_path, bucket_name, object_key, ExtraArgs={&#x27;ACL&#x27;: &#x27;public-read&#x27;})\n    print(f&quot;Uploaded {file_path} to s3://{bucket_name}/{object_key}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    upload_to_s3(&#x27;local_file.txt&#x27;, &#x27;my-bucket&#x27;, &#x27;public_file.txt&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0019","card":"q-boto3-004-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"Use a specific profile from <code>~/.aws/credentials</code>.","a":"<p>Create a <code>boto3.session.Session(profile_name=...)</code> and build clients from the session.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\nsession = boto3.session.Session(profile_name=&#x27;my-profile&#x27;)\ns3 = session.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\nresponse = s3.list_buckets()\nprint(response[&#x27;Buckets&#x27;])</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0020","card":"q-boto3-004-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"Start, stop, terminate EC2.","a":"<p><code>start_instances</code>, <code>stop_instances</code>, <code>terminate_instances</code>, each with <code>InstanceIds</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef manage_ec2_instance(instance_id, action):\n    ec2 = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;)\n    if action == &#x27;start&#x27;:\n        ec2.start_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n        print(f&quot;Starting instance {instance_id}&quot;)\n    elif action == &#x27;stop&#x27;:\n        ec2.stop_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n        print(f&quot;Stopping instance {instance_id}&quot;)\n    elif action == &#x27;terminate&#x27;:\n        ec2.terminate_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n        print(f&quot;Terminating instance {instance_id}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    manage_ec2_instance(&#x27;i-1234567890abcdef0&#x27;, &#x27;start&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0021","card":"q-boto3-005-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"Create an SNS topic and publish.","a":"<p><code>create_topic</code> returns the <code>TopicArn</code>, which <code>publish</code> needs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef create_and_publish_sns(topic_name, message):\n    sns = boto3.client(&#x27;sns&#x27;)\n    response = sns.create_topic(Name=topic_name)\n    topic_arn = response[&#x27;TopicArn&#x27;]\n    sns.publish(TopicArn=topic_arn, Message=message)\n    print(f&quot;Published message to {topic_arn}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    create_and_publish_sns(&#x27;my-topic&#x27;, &#x27;Hello, SNS!&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0022","card":"q-boto3-005-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"Query DynamoDB and do conditional writes.","a":"<p>Use the DynamoDB resource; <code>put_item</code> with <code>ConditionExpression</code> fails with <code>ClientError</code> when the condition is false.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\n\ndef query_and_write_dynamodb(table_name, item_key, item_data):\n    dynamodb = boto3.resource(&#x27;dynamodb&#x27;)\n    table = dynamodb.Table(table_name)\n\n    # Query\n    response = table.query(KeyConditionExpression=&#x27;id = :id&#x27;, ExpressionAttributeValues={&#x27;:id&#x27;: item_key})\n    print(f&quot;Query results: {response[&#x27;Items&#x27;]}&quot;)\n\n    # Conditional write\n    try:\n        table.put_item(Item={&#x27;id&#x27;: item_key, &#x27;data&#x27;: item_data}, ConditionExpression=&#x27;attribute_not_exists(id)&#x27;)\n        print(&quot;Item written successfully&quot;)\n    except ClientError as e:\n        print(f&quot;Conditional write failed: {e}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    query_and_write_dynamodb(&#x27;my-table&#x27;, &#x27;123&#x27;, &#x27;example-data&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0023","card":"q-boto3-005-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"Create a Lambda function and invoke it.","a":"<p>Zip the code in memory, <code>create_function</code> with a role ARN and handler, then <code>invoke</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport zipfile\nimport io\n\ndef create_and_invoke_lambda(function_name):\n    lambda_client = boto3.client(&#x27;lambda&#x27;)\n\n    # Create ZIP file for Lambda code\n    zip_buffer = io.BytesIO()\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(zip_buffer, &#x27;a&#x27;, zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as zf:\n        zf.writestr(&#x27;index.py&#x27;, &#x27;def handler(event, context):\\n    return {&quot;statusCode&quot;: 200, &quot;body&quot;: &quot;Hello from Lambda!&quot;}&#x27;)\n    zip_buffer.seek(0)\n\n    # Create Lambda function\n    lambda_client.create_function(\n        FunctionName=function_name,\n        Runtime=&#x27;python3.9&#x27;,\n        Role=&#x27;arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/lambda-role&#x27;,\n        Handler=&#x27;index.handler&#x27;,\n        Code={&#x27;ZipFile&#x27;: zip_buffer.read()}\n    )\n\n    # Invoke Lambda\n    response = lambda_client.invoke(FunctionName=function_name)\n    print(f&quot;Lambda response: {response[&#x27;Payload&#x27;].read().decode()}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    create_and_invoke_lambda(&#x27;my-lambda&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0024","card":"q-boto3-006-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"Manage IAM roles and policies.","a":"<p>IAM client: create roles and policies; <code>attach_role_policy</code> attaches one.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef attach_policy_to_role(role_name, policy_arn):\n    iam = boto3.client(&#x27;iam&#x27;)\n    iam.attach_role_policy(RoleName=role_name, PolicyArn=policy_arn)\n    print(f&quot;Attached {policy_arn} to {role_name}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    attach_policy_to_role(&#x27;my-role&#x27;, &#x27;arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0025","card":"q-boto3-006-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"CloudFormation stacks.","a":"<p><code>create_stack</code>, <code>update_stack</code>, <code>delete_stack</code>. Use a waiter to block until done. (The source example shows only create plus waiter.)</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef manage_cloudformation_stack(stack_name, template_body):\n    cf = boto3.client(&#x27;cloudformation&#x27;)\n    cf.create_stack(StackName=stack_name, TemplateBody=template_body)\n    cf.get_waiter(&#x27;stack_create_complete&#x27;).wait(StackName=stack_name)\n    print(f&quot;Stack {stack_name} created&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    template = &#x27;&#x27;&#x27;\n    Resources:\n      MyBucket:\n        Type: AWS::S3::Bucket\n    &#x27;&#x27;&#x27;\n    manage_cloudformation_stack(&#x27;my-stack&#x27;, template)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0026","card":"q-boto3-006-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"Monitor CloudWatch metrics for an EC2 instance.","a":"<p><code>get_metric_statistics</code> with namespace, metric, dimensions, time range, period and statistic.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef monitor_ec2_metrics(instance_id):\n    cloudwatch = boto3.client(&#x27;cloudwatch&#x27;)\n    response = cloudwatch.get_metric_statistics(\n        Namespace=&#x27;AWS/EC2&#x27;,\n        MetricName=&#x27;CPUUtilization&#x27;,\n        Dimensions=[{&#x27;Name&#x27;: &#x27;InstanceId&#x27;, &#x27;Value&#x27;: instance_id}],\n        StartTime=datetime.utcnow() - timedelta(minutes=60),\n        EndTime=datetime.utcnow(),\n        Period=300,\n        Statistics=[&#x27;Average&#x27;]\n    )\n    for datapoint in response[&#x27;Datapoints&#x27;]:\n        print(f&quot;Time: {datapoint[&#x27;Timestamp&#x27;]}, CPU: {datapoint[&#x27;Average&#x27;]}%&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    monitor_ec2_metrics(&#x27;i-1234567890abcdef0&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0027","card":"q-boto3-007-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"Throttling and rate limits.","a":"<p>Exponential backoff, either through boto3's retry configuration or manual retries.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\nimport time\n\ndef list_objects_with_retry(bucket_name):\n    s3 = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    retries = 3\n    for attempt in range(retries):\n        try:\n            response = s3.list_objects_v2(Bucket=bucket_name)\n            return response[&#x27;Contents&#x27;]\n        except ClientError as e:\n            if e.response[&#x27;Error&#x27;][&#x27;Code&#x27;] == &#x27;Throttling&#x27; and attempt &lt; retries - 1:\n                time.sleep(2 ** attempt)\n            else:\n                raise\n    return []\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    objects = list_objects_with_retry(&#x27;my-bucket&#x27;)\n    print(objects)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0028","card":"q-boto3-007-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"Create an SQS queue and send a message.","a":"<p><code>create_queue</code> returns <code>QueueUrl</code>, which <code>send_message</code> needs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef create_and_send_sqs_message(queue_name, message):\n    sqs = boto3.client(&#x27;sqs&#x27;)\n    response = sqs.create_queue(QueueName=queue_name)\n    queue_url = response[&#x27;QueueUrl&#x27;]\n    sqs.send_message(QueueUrl=queue_url, MessageBody=message)\n    print(f&quot;Sent message to {queue_url}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    create_and_send_sqs_message(&#x27;my-queue&#x27;, &#x27;Hello, SQS!&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0029","card":"q-boto3-007-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"VPC subnet and security group.","a":"<p>VPC resources are created through the EC2 client.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef create_vpc_resources(vpc_id):\n    ec2 = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;)\n    subnet = ec2.create_subnet(VpcId=vpc_id, CidrBlock=&#x27;10.0.1.0/24&#x27;)\n    sg = ec2.create_security_group(GroupName=&#x27;my-sg&#x27;, Description=&#x27;My security group&#x27;, VpcId=vpc_id)\n    print(f&quot;Created subnet: {subnet[&#x27;Subnet&#x27;][&#x27;SubnetId&#x27;]}, SG: {sg[&#x27;GroupId&#x27;]}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    create_vpc_resources(&#x27;vpc-12345678&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0030","card":"q-boto3-007-2-core-aws-services-with-boto3-q16-30","sec":"boto3-s003","q":"STS assume role for cross-account access.","a":"<p><code>assume_role</code> returns temporary <code>AccessKeyId</code>, <code>SecretAccessKey</code> and <code>SessionToken</code>; pass them to a new client.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef assume_role(role_arn, session_name):\n    sts = boto3.client(&#x27;sts&#x27;)\n    response = sts.assume_role(RoleArn=role_arn, RoleSessionName=session_name)\n    credentials = response[&#x27;Credentials&#x27;]\n    s3 = boto3.client(\n        &#x27;s3&#x27;,\n        aws_access_key_id=credentials[&#x27;AccessKeyId&#x27;],\n        aws_secret_access_key=credentials[&#x27;SecretAccessKey&#x27;],\n        aws_session_token=credentials[&#x27;SessionToken&#x27;]\n    )\n    buckets = s3.list_buckets()\n    print(buckets[&#x27;Buckets&#x27;])\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    assume_role(&#x27;arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/MyRole&#x27;, &#x27;MySession&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0031","card":"q-boto3-008-3-boto3-with-eks-kubernetes-q31-40","sec":"boto3-s004","q":"Get EKS cluster details.","a":"<p><code>describe_cluster</code> returns status, endpoint, version.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef get_eks_cluster_details(cluster_name, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    eks_client = boto3.client(&#x27;eks&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    response = eks_client.describe_cluster(name=cluster_name)\n    return response[&#x27;cluster&#x27;]\n\n# Example usage\ncluster_details = get_eks_cluster_details(&#x27;my-eks-cluster&#x27;)\nprint(f&quot;Cluster Name: {cluster_details[&#x27;name&#x27;]}, Status: {cluster_details[&#x27;status&#x27;]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0032","card":"q-boto3-008-3-boto3-with-eks-kubernetes-q31-40","sec":"boto3-s004","q":"List EKS clusters in a region.","a":"<p><code>list_clusters</code> with a paginator.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef list_eks_clusters(region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    eks_client = boto3.client(&#x27;eks&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    clusters = []\n    paginator = eks_client.get_paginator(&#x27;list_clusters&#x27;)\n    for page in paginator.paginate():\n        clusters.extend(page[&#x27;clusters&#x27;])\n    return clusters\n\n# Example usage\nclusters = list_eks_clusters()\nfor cluster in clusters:\n    print(f&quot;Cluster: {cluster}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0033","card":"q-boto3-008-3-boto3-with-eks-kubernetes-q31-40","sec":"boto3-s004","q":"Update cluster config (scale a node group).","a":"<p><code>update_nodegroup_config</code> with <code>scalingConfig</code>; needs the cluster and node group names.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef scale_eks_nodegroup(cluster_name, nodegroup_name, desired_size, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    eks_client = boto3.client(&#x27;eks&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    response = eks_client.update_nodegroup_config(\n        clusterName=cluster_name,\n        nodegroupName=nodegroup_name,\n        scalingConfig={\n            &#x27;minSize&#x27;: desired_size,\n            &#x27;maxSize&#x27;: desired_size + 2,\n            &#x27;desiredSize&#x27;: desired_size\n        }\n    )\n    return response\n\n# Example usage\nresponse = scale_eks_nodegroup(&#x27;my-eks-cluster&#x27;, &#x27;my-nodegroup&#x27;, 3)\nprint(f&quot;Nodegroup update initiated: {response[&#x27;update&#x27;][&#x27;id&#x27;]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0034","card":"q-boto3-008-3-boto3-with-eks-kubernetes-q31-40","sec":"boto3-s004","q":"IAM roles for EKS service accounts (IRSA).","a":"<p>Create a role whose trust policy lets the cluster's OIDC provider assume it via <code>sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity</code>, scoped to one service account, then attach policies. Annotate the Kubernetes service account with the role ARN.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport json\n\ndef create_eks_service_account_role(role_name, cluster_name, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    iam_client = boto3.client(&#x27;iam&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    trust_policy = {\n        &quot;Version&quot;: &quot;2012-10-17&quot;,\n        &quot;Statement&quot;: [\n            {\n                &quot;Effect&quot;: &quot;Allow&quot;,\n                &quot;Principal&quot;: {&quot;Federated&quot;: f&quot;arn:aws:iam::123456789012:oidc-provider/oidc.eks.{region}.amazonaws.com/id/EXAMPLED539D4633E53DE1B716D3041E&quot;},\n                &quot;Action&quot;: &quot;sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity&quot;,\n                &quot;Condition&quot;: {\n                    &quot;StringEquals&quot;: {\n                        f&quot;oidc.eks.{region}.amazonaws.com/id/EXAMPLED539D4633E53DE1B716D3041E:sub&quot;: &quot;system:serviceaccount:default:my-sa&quot;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        ]\n    }\n    response = iam_client.create_role(\n        RoleName=role_name,\n        AssumeRolePolicyDocument=json.dumps(trust_policy)\n    )\n    iam_client.attach_role_policy(\n        RoleName=role_name,\n        PolicyArn=&#x27;arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess&#x27;\n    )\n    return response[&#x27;Role&#x27;][&#x27;Arn&#x27;]\n\n# Example usage\nrole_arn = create_eks_service_account_role(&#x27;eks-sa-role&#x27;, &#x27;my-eks-cluster&#x27;)\nprint(f&quot;Role ARN: {role_arn}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0035","card":"q-boto3-009-3-boto3-with-eks-kubernetes-q31-40","sec":"boto3-s004","q":"Create a node group.","a":"<p><code>create_nodegroup</code> takes instance types, scaling config, subnets and the node IAM role.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef create_eks_nodegroup(cluster_name, nodegroup_name, role_arn, subnets, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    eks_client = boto3.client(&#x27;eks&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    response = eks_client.create_nodegroup(\n        clusterName=cluster_name,\n        nodegroupName=nodegroup_name,\n        scalingConfig={\n            &#x27;minSize&#x27;: 1,\n            &#x27;maxSize&#x27;: 3,\n            &#x27;desiredSize&#x27;: 2\n        },\n        instanceTypes=[&#x27;t3.medium&#x27;],\n        subnets=subnets,\n        nodeRole=role_arn\n    )\n    return response\n\n# Example usage\nresponse = create_eks_nodegroup(\n    &#x27;my-eks-cluster&#x27;, \n    &#x27;my-nodegroup&#x27;, \n    &#x27;arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/EKSNodeRole&#x27;, \n    [&#x27;subnet-12345678&#x27;, &#x27;subnet-87654321&#x27;]\n)\nprint(f&quot;Nodegroup creation initiated: {response[&#x27;nodegroup&#x27;][&#x27;nodegroupArn&#x27;]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0036","card":"q-boto3-009-3-boto3-with-eks-kubernetes-q31-40","sec":"boto3-s004","q":"Combine boto3 with the <code>kubernetes</code> client.","a":"<p>boto3 fetches the cluster endpoint and CA data; those configure the Kubernetes API client. (Gotcha: the source passes the caller ARN as the API key. Real EKS auth needs a signed STS token, for example from <code>aws eks get-token</code>.)</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nfrom kubernetes import client, config\nfrom kubernetes.client.rest import ApiException\n\ndef configure_k8s_client(cluster_name, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    eks_client = boto3.client(&#x27;eks&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    cluster = eks_client.describe_cluster(name=cluster_name)[&#x27;cluster&#x27;]\n    configuration = client.Configuration()\n    configuration.host = cluster[&#x27;endpoint&#x27;]\n    configuration.ssl_ca_cert = cluster[&#x27;certificateAuthority&#x27;][&#x27;data&#x27;]\n    configuration.api_key[&#x27;authorization&#x27;] = boto3.client(&#x27;sts&#x27;).get_caller_identity()[&#x27;Arn&#x27;]\n    k8s_client = client.ApiClient(configuration)\n    return client.CoreV1Api(k8s_client)\n\n# Example usage: List pods\nk8s_api = configure_k8s_client(&#x27;my-eks-cluster&#x27;)\npods = k8s_api.list_pod_for_all_namespaces()\nfor pod in pods.items:\n    print(f&quot;Pod: {pod.metadata.name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0037","card":"q-boto3-010-3-boto3-with-eks-kubernetes-q31-40","sec":"boto3-s004","q":"Retrieve EKS logs from CloudWatch.","a":"<p>Use the <code>logs</code> client against the log group <code>/aws/eks/&lt;cluster&gt;/cluster</code>; times are epoch milliseconds.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\n\ndef get_eks_logs(cluster_name, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    logs_client = boto3.client(&#x27;logs&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    log_group = f&quot;/aws/eks/{cluster_name}/cluster&quot;\n    response = logs_client.filter_log_events(\n        logGroupName=log_group,\n        startTime=int((datetime.now() - timedelta(hours=1)).timestamp() * 1000),\n        endTime=int(datetime.now().timestamp() * 1000)\n    )\n    return response[&#x27;events&#x27;]\n\n# Example usage\nlogs = get_eks_logs(&#x27;my-eks-cluster&#x27;)\nfor log in logs:\n    print(f&quot;Log: {log[&#x27;message&#x27;]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0038","card":"q-boto3-010-3-boto3-with-eks-kubernetes-q31-40","sec":"boto3-s004","q":"Configure autoscaling for EKS.","a":"<p>Same <code>update_nodegroup_config</code> call as Q33, with <code>minSize</code>/<code>maxSize</code> set to the autoscaling bounds and <code>desiredSize</code> set to the minimum: <code>configure_eks_autoscaling(cluster, nodegroup, 2, 5)</code>. The <code>autoscaling</code> client can also tune the underlying Auto Scaling group. This call only sets bounds; actual scale-out needs the Cluster Autoscaler (see Q78).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0039","card":"q-boto3-010-3-boto3-with-eks-kubernetes-q31-40","sec":"boto3-s004","q":"Delete an EKS cluster and its resources.","a":"<p>Delete node groups first, wait, then delete the cluster.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport time\n\ndef delete_eks_cluster(cluster_name, nodegroup_name, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    eks_client = boto3.client(&#x27;eks&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    # Delete node group\n    eks_client.delete_nodegroup(clusterName=cluster_name, nodegroupName=nodegroup_name)\n    while eks_client.describe_nodegroup(clusterName=cluster_name, nodegroupName=nodegroup_name)[&#x27;nodegroup&#x27;][&#x27;status&#x27;] != &#x27;DELETED&#x27;:\n        print(&quot;Waiting for nodegroup deletion...&quot;)\n        time.sleep(30)\n    # Delete cluster\n    eks_client.delete_cluster(name=cluster_name)\n    while eks_client.describe_cluster(name=cluster_name)[&#x27;cluster&#x27;][&#x27;status&#x27;] != &#x27;DELETED&#x27;:\n        print(&quot;Waiting for cluster deletion...&quot;)\n        time.sleep(30)\n    print(&quot;Cluster and nodegroup deleted.&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\ndelete_eks_cluster(&#x27;my-eks-cluster&#x27;, &#x27;my-nodegroup&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0040","card":"q-boto3-010-3-boto3-with-eks-kubernetes-q31-40","sec":"boto3-s004","q":"Manage EKS add-ons (VPC-CNI, CoreDNS).","a":"<p><code>create_addon</code>, <code>describe_addon</code>, <code>delete_addon</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef manage_eks_addon(cluster_name, addon_name, version, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    eks_client = boto3.client(&#x27;eks&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    response = eks_client.create_addon(\n        clusterName=cluster_name,\n        addonName=addon_name,\n        addonVersion=version\n    )\n    return response\n\n# Example usage\nresponse = manage_eks_addon(&#x27;my-eks-cluster&#x27;, &#x27;vpc-cni&#x27;, &#x27;v1.10.1-eksbuild.1&#x27;)\nprint(f&quot;Addon created: {response[&#x27;addon&#x27;][&#x27;addonArn&#x27;]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0041","card":"q-boto3-011-4-boto3-with-terraform-q41-50","sec":"boto3-s005","q":"Validate or inspect Terraform-created resources.","a":"<p>Query AWS and compare tags or attributes with what Terraform expects.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef validate_terraform_resources(resource_type, expected_tags):\n    client = boto3.client(resource_type)\n    if resource_type == &#x27;ec2&#x27;:\n        response = client.describe_instances()\n        for reservation in response[&#x27;Reservations&#x27;]:\n            for instance in reservation[&#x27;Instances&#x27;]:\n                tags = {tag[&#x27;Key&#x27;]: tag[&#x27;Value&#x27;] for tag in instance.get(&#x27;Tags&#x27;, [])}\n                if all(tag in tags.items() for tag in expected_tags.items()):\n                    print(f&quot;Validated EC2 instance: {instance[&#x27;InstanceId&#x27;]}&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\nvalidate_terraform_resources(&#x27;ec2&#x27;, {&#x27;Terraform&#x27;: &#x27;true&#x27;, &#x27;Environment&#x27;: &#x27;dev&#x27;})</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0042","card":"q-boto3-011-4-boto3-with-terraform-q41-50","sec":"boto3-s005","q":"List resources from a Terraform state file.","a":"<p>Parse the state, then verify each resource exists in AWS.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport json\n\ndef list_terraform_resources(state_file_path):\n    with open(state_file_path, &#x27;r&#x27;) as f:\n        state = json.load(f)\n    resources = state[&#x27;resources&#x27;]\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;)\n    for resource in resources:\n        if resource[&#x27;type&#x27;] == &#x27;aws_instance&#x27;:\n            instance_id = resource[&#x27;instances&#x27;][0][&#x27;attributes&#x27;][&#x27;id&#x27;]\n            response = ec2_client.describe_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n            print(f&quot;Found EC2 instance: {instance_id}&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\nlist_terraform_resources(&#x27;terraform.tfstate&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0043","card":"q-boto3-011-4-boto3-with-terraform-q41-50","sec":"boto3-s005","q":"Post-provisioning tasks.","a":"<p>Tag, start/stop, or adjust security groups after Terraform creates the resource.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef configure_ec2_instance(instance_id, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    ec2_client.create_tags(\n        Resources=[instance_id],\n        Tags=[{&#x27;Key&#x27;: &#x27;PostConfigured&#x27;, &#x27;Value&#x27;: &#x27;true&#x27;}]\n    )\n    ec2_client.start_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n    print(f&quot;Configured and started EC2 instance: {instance_id}&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\nconfigure_ec2_instance(&#x27;i-1234567890abcdef0&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0044","card":"q-boto3-011-4-boto3-with-terraform-q41-50","sec":"boto3-s005","q":"Terraform-managed S3 buckets for state storage.","a":"<p>Enable versioning, encryption, or check that the state file exists.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef manage_terraform_s3_backend(bucket_name, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    s3_client.put_bucket_versioning(\n        Bucket=bucket_name,\n        VersioningConfiguration={&#x27;Status&#x27;: &#x27;Enabled&#x27;}\n    )\n    response = s3_client.list_objects_v2(Bucket=bucket_name, Prefix=&#x27;terraform.tfstate&#x27;)\n    if &#x27;Contents&#x27; in response:\n        print(f&quot;Terraform state file found in {bucket_name}&quot;)\n    else:\n        print(f&quot;No state file found in {bucket_name}&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\nmanage_terraform_s3_backend(&#x27;my-terraform-backend&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0045","card":"q-boto3-012-4-boto3-with-terraform-q41-50","sec":"boto3-s005","q":"Check a Terraform-managed CloudFormation stack's status.","a":"<p><code>describe_stacks</code>, read <code>StackStatus</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef check_cloudformation_stack(stack_name, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    cf_client = boto3.client(&#x27;cloudformation&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    response = cf_client.describe_stacks(StackName=stack_name)\n    stack = response[&#x27;Stacks&#x27;][0]\n    print(f&quot;Stack {stack_name} Status: {stack[&#x27;StackStatus&#x27;]}&quot;)\n    return stack[&#x27;StackStatus&#x27;]\n\n# Example usage\ncheck_cloudformation_stack(&#x27;my-terraform-stack&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0046","card":"q-boto3-012-4-boto3-with-terraform-q41-50","sec":"boto3-s005","q":"Trigger Terraform programmatically (Lambda).","a":"<p>A Lambda function (S3 trigger or API call) downloads the config and runs <code>terraform apply</code> through a subprocess, or delegates to AWS CodeBuild. (Practical gotcha: the Terraform binary must be packaged in the Lambda.)</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport subprocess\n\ndef lambda_handler(event, context):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    s3_client.download_file(&#x27;my-terraform-bucket&#x27;, &#x27;terraform/main.tf&#x27;, &#x27;/tmp/main.tf&#x27;)\n    result = subprocess.run([&#x27;terraform&#x27;, &#x27;apply&#x27;, &#x27;-auto-approve&#x27;], cwd=&#x27;/tmp&#x27;, capture_output=True)\n    return {\n        &#x27;statusCode&#x27;: 200,\n        &#x27;body&#x27;: result.stdout.decode()\n    }</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0047","card":"q-boto3-012-4-boto3-with-terraform-q41-50","sec":"boto3-s005","q":"Clean up orphaned resources not in Terraform.","a":"<p>List live resources, compare against state IDs, delete the unmanaged ones. Destructive: dry-run first (Q85).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport json\n\ndef clean_orphaned_resources(state_file_path, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    with open(state_file_path, &#x27;r&#x27;) as f:\n        state = json.load(f)\n    managed_ids = [r[&#x27;instances&#x27;][0][&#x27;attributes&#x27;][&#x27;id&#x27;] for r in state[&#x27;resources&#x27;] if r[&#x27;type&#x27;] == &#x27;aws_instance&#x27;]\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    response = ec2_client.describe_instances()\n    for reservation in response[&#x27;Reservations&#x27;]:\n        for instance in reservation[&#x27;Instances&#x27;]:\n            if instance[&#x27;InstanceId&#x27;] not in managed_ids:\n                ec2_client.terminate_instances(InstanceIds=[instance[&#x27;InstanceId&#x27;]])\n                print(f&quot;Terminated orphaned instance: {instance[&#x27;InstanceId&#x27;]}&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\nclean_orphaned_resources(&#x27;terraform.tfstate&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0048","card":"q-boto3-013-4-boto3-with-terraform-q41-50","sec":"boto3-s005","q":"Enable versioning on the backend bucket.","a":"<p>Same <code>put_bucket_versioning(Bucket=..., VersioningConfiguration={'Status': 'Enabled'})</code> call as Q44, on its own.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0049","card":"q-boto3-013-4-boto3-with-terraform-q41-50","sec":"boto3-s005","q":"Dynamic credentials for Terraform's AWS provider.","a":"<p>Assume a role via STS, then export the temporary credentials as environment variables, which the provider reads. (Q60 for Ansible is the same code with <code>RoleSessionName='AnsibleSession'</code>.)</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport os\n\ndef set_terraform_credentials(role_arn, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    sts_client = boto3.client(&#x27;sts&#x27;)\n    response = sts_client.assume_role(RoleArn=role_arn, RoleSessionName=&#x27;TerraformSession&#x27;)\n    credentials = response[&#x27;Credentials&#x27;]\n    os.environ[&#x27;AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID&#x27;] = credentials[&#x27;AccessKeyId&#x27;]\n    os.environ[&#x27;AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY&#x27;] = credentials[&#x27;SecretAccessKey&#x27;]\n    os.environ[&#x27;AWS_SESSION_TOKEN&#x27;] = credentials[&#x27;SessionToken&#x27;]\n    print(&quot;Terraform credentials set.&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\nset_terraform_credentials(&#x27;arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/TerraformRole&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0050","card":"q-boto3-013-4-boto3-with-terraform-q41-50","sec":"boto3-s005","q":"Monitor drift.","a":"<p>Compare live attributes (tags, instance type, security groups) with the state file.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport json\n\ndef detect_drift(state_file_path, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    with open(state_file_path, &#x27;r&#x27;) as f:\n        state = json.load(f)\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    for resource in state[&#x27;resources&#x27;]:\n        if resource[&#x27;type&#x27;] == &#x27;aws_instance&#x27;:\n            instance_id = resource[&#x27;instances&#x27;][0][&#x27;attributes&#x27;][&#x27;id&#x27;]\n            response = ec2_client.describe_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n            actual_tags = response[&#x27;Reservations&#x27;][0][&#x27;Instances&#x27;][0].get(&#x27;Tags&#x27;, [])\n            expected_tags = resource[&#x27;instances&#x27;][0][&#x27;attributes&#x27;][&#x27;tags&#x27;]\n            if actual_tags != expected_tags:\n                print(f&quot;Drift detected for instance {instance_id}: Tags differ&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\ndetect_drift(&#x27;terraform.tfstate&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0051","card":"q-boto3-014-5-boto3-with-ansible-q51-60","sec":"boto3-s006","q":"Complement Ansible playbooks.","a":"<p>Create or query resources before or after playbooks run.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef prepare_aws_resources():\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;)\n    response = ec2_client.run_instances(\n        ImageId=&#x27;ami-12345678&#x27;,\n        InstanceType=&#x27;t2.micro&#x27;,\n        MinCount=1,\n        MaxCount=1\n    )\n    instance_id = response[&#x27;Instances&#x27;][0][&#x27;InstanceId&#x27;]\n    print(f&quot;Created instance: {instance_id}&quot;)\n    return instance_id\n\n# Example usage\ninstance_id = prepare_aws_resources()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0052","card":"q-boto3-014-5-boto3-with-ansible-q51-60","sec":"boto3-s006","q":"Generate an inventory for Ansible.","a":"<p>Query running instances and write them in an inventory-compatible structure.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport json\n\ndef generate_ansible_inventory(region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    response = ec2_client.describe_instances()\n    inventory = {&#x27;webservers&#x27;: {&#x27;hosts&#x27;: []}}\n    for reservation in response[&#x27;Reservations&#x27;]:\n        for instance in reservation[&#x27;Instances&#x27;]:\n            if instance[&#x27;State&#x27;][&#x27;Name&#x27;] == &#x27;running&#x27;:\n                inventory[&#x27;webservers&#x27;][&#x27;hosts&#x27;].append(instance[&#x27;PublicIpAddress&#x27;])\n    with open(&#x27;inventory.json&#x27;, &#x27;w&#x27;) as f:\n        json.dump(inventory, f)\n    print(&quot;Ansible inventory generated.&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\ngenerate_ansible_inventory()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0053","card":"q-boto3-014-5-boto3-with-ansible-q51-60","sec":"boto3-s006","q":"Validate resource state before a playbook.","a":"<p>Check instance state or tags so prerequisites are met.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef validate_aws_resources(instance_id, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    response = ec2_client.describe_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n    instance = response[&#x27;Reservations&#x27;][0][&#x27;Instances&#x27;][0]\n    if instance[&#x27;State&#x27;][&#x27;Name&#x27;] != &#x27;running&#x27;:\n        raise Exception(f&quot;Instance {instance_id} is not running&quot;)\n    print(f&quot;Instance {instance_id} is ready for Ansible playbook&quot;)\n    return True\n\n# Example usage\nvalidate_aws_resources(&#x27;i-1234567890abcdef0&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0054","card":"q-boto3-014-5-boto3-with-ansible-q51-60","sec":"boto3-s006","q":"Create resources Ansible will configure.","a":"<p>Provision EC2 or S3 with boto3, then pass IDs/ARNs to Ansible. Code is the same as Q51 (<code>run_instances</code>, return <code>instance_id</code>), with a <code>region</code> parameter.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0055","card":"q-boto3-015-5-boto3-with-ansible-q51-60","sec":"boto3-s006","q":"Tag instances for Ansible dynamic inventory.","a":"<p><code>create_tags</code>; Ansible groups hosts by tag.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef tag_ec2_instances(instance_ids, tags, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    ec2_client.create_tags(\n        Resources=instance_ids,\n        Tags=[{&#x27;Key&#x27;: k, &#x27;Value&#x27;: v} for k, v in tags.items()]\n    )\n    print(f&quot;Tagged instances: {instance_ids}&quot;)\n\n# Example usage\ntag_ec2_instances([&#x27;i-1234567890abcdef0&#x27;], {&#x27;AnsibleGroup&#x27;: &#x27;webservers&#x27;})</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0056","card":"q-boto3-015-5-boto3-with-ansible-q51-60","sec":"boto3-s006","q":"Ensure prerequisites (boto3 installed) for Ansible's AWS modules.","a":"<p>Run a shell command on the instance through SSM <code>send_command</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef ensure_ansible_prerequisites(instance_id, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    ssm_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ssm&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    response = ssm_client.send_command(\n        InstanceIds=[instance_id],\n        DocumentName=&#x27;AWS-RunShellScript&#x27;,\n        Parameters={&#x27;commands&#x27;: [&#x27;pip install boto3&#x27;]}\n    )\n    print(f&quot;Ensured boto3 installation on {instance_id}&quot;)\n    return response[&#x27;Command&#x27;][&#x27;CommandId&#x27;]\n\n# Example usage\nensure_ansible_prerequisites(&#x27;i-1234567890abcdef0&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0057","card":"q-boto3-015-5-boto3-with-ansible-q51-60","sec":"boto3-s006","q":"Retrieve resource details for Ansible's <code>ec2_instance</code> module.","a":"<p>Query with boto3 and save to a JSON file or environment variables. (Gotcha: the source code uses <code>json.dump</code> without <code>import json</code>.)</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef get_ec2_details(instance_id, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    response = ec2_client.describe_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n    instance = response[&#x27;Reservations&#x27;][0][&#x27;Instances&#x27;][0]\n    details = {\n        &#x27;instance_id&#x27;: instance[&#x27;InstanceId&#x27;],\n        &#x27;public_ip&#x27;: instance.get(&#x27;PublicIpAddress&#x27;, &#x27;N/A&#x27;)\n    }\n    with open(&#x27;ec2_details.json&#x27;, &#x27;w&#x27;) as f:\n        json.dump(details, f)\n    print(f&quot;EC2 details saved for Ansible&quot;)\n    return details\n\n# Example usage\nget_ec2_details(&#x27;i-1234567890abcdef0&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0058","card":"q-boto3-015-5-boto3-with-ansible-q51-60","sec":"boto3-s006","q":"Create an SNS topic for Ansible notifications.","a":"<p><code>create_topic</code> and return the ARN; same call as Q21, with a <code>region</code> parameter and a <code>return topic_arn</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0059","card":"q-boto3-015-5-boto3-with-ansible-q51-60","sec":"boto3-s006","q":"Handle resource failures dynamically.","a":"<p>Monitor health (for example via CloudWatch) and remediate, either by restarting directly or by triggering an Ansible playbook.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef handle_ec2_failure(instance_id, region=&#x27;us-east-1&#x27;):\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;, region_name=region)\n    response = ec2_client.describe_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n    if response[&#x27;Reservations&#x27;][0][&#x27;Instances&#x27;][0][&#x27;State&#x27;][&#x27;Name&#x27;] != &#x27;running&#x27;:\n        ec2_client.start_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n        print(f&quot;Restarted failed instance: {instance_id}&quot;)\n    return True\n\n# Example usage\nhandle_ec2_failure(&#x27;i-1234567890abcdef0&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0060","card":"q-boto3-016-5-boto3-with-ansible-q51-60","sec":"boto3-s006","q":"Secure credentials for Ansible's AWS modules.","a":"<p>Use STS temporary credentials or an assumed role, passed via environment variables or a credentials file. Code is the same as Q49 with <code>RoleSessionName='AnsibleSession'</code> and role <code>.../role/AnsibleRole</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0061","card":"q-boto3-017-6-boto3-with-github-actions-q61-70","sec":"boto3-s007","q":"How is boto3 used in GitHub Actions?","a":"<p>A workflow step sets up Python, installs boto3, configures AWS credentials and runs a script that creates, updates or deletes resources. Credentials come from GitHub Secrets, or better from an IAM role through OIDC.</p>\n<p><strong>Standard workflow skeleton.</strong> Almost every workflow in Q62-70 repeats these steps; only the trigger, an extra step, and the final <code>run:</code> line change (see the variants below).</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0062","card":"q-boto3-017-6-boto3-with-github-actions-q61-70","sec":"boto3-s007","q":"Deploy a Lambda function (workflow + script).","a":"<p>The script uploads the zip to S3, then <code>update_function_code</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>name: Deploy Lambda Function\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\njobs:\n  deploy:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n    - uses: actions/checkout@v3\n    - name: Set up Python\n      uses: actions/setup-python@v4\n      with:\n        python-version: &#x27;3.10&#x27;\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: pip install boto3\n    - name: Zip Lambda code\n      run: zip -r lambda_function.zip lambda_function.py\n    - name: Configure AWS Credentials\n      uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v2\n      with:\n        aws-access-key-id: ${{ secrets.AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID }}\n        aws-secret-access-key: ${{ secrets.AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY }}\n        aws-region: us-east-1\n    - name: Deploy Lambda\n      run: python deploy_lambda.py</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># deploy_lambda.py\nimport boto3\n\ndef deploy_lambda():\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    lambda_client = boto3.client(&#x27;lambda&#x27;)\n    bucket_name = &#x27;my-lambda-bucket&#x27;\n    function_name = &#x27;MyLambdaFunction&#x27;\n\n    # Upload zip to S3\n    s3_client.upload_file(&#x27;lambda_function.zip&#x27;, bucket_name, &#x27;lambda_function.zip&#x27;)\n\n    # Update Lambda function code\n    lambda_client.update_function_code(\n        FunctionName=function_name,\n        S3Bucket=bucket_name,\n        S3Key=&#x27;lambda_function.zip&#x27;\n    )\n    print(f&quot;Updated Lambda function: {function_name}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    deploy_lambda()</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0063","card":"q-boto3-017-6-boto3-with-github-actions-q61-70","sec":"boto3-s007","q":"Configure AWS credentials securely.","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Store <code>AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID</code> and <code>AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY</code> in GitHub Secrets.</li>\n  <li>Set them with the <code>aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials</code> action (the step shown in Q62).</li>\n  <li>Prefer IAM roles with temporary credentials via OIDC (see Q76).</li>\n  <li>Never hardcode credentials in scripts or workflow files.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Workflow variants for Q64-70.</strong> Each of these uses the Q62 skeleton, with these differences:</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># Q64 validate S3: on: [push]; final step\n    - name: Validate S3\n      run: python validate_s3.py\n\n# Q65 scale EKS: manual trigger; final step\non: [workflow_dispatch]\n    - name: Scale EKS\n      run: python scale_eks.py\n\n# Q66 publish test results to SNS: extra steps before/after credentials\n    - name: Install dependencies\n      run: pip install boto3 pytest\n    - name: Run tests\n      run: pytest --junitxml=report.xml\n    - name: Publish to SNS\n      run: python publish_sns.py\n\n# Q67 create S3 bucket + upload; Q68 CloudFormation deploy: final steps\n    - name: Create and Upload to S3\n      run: python s3_upload.py\n    - name: Deploy Stack\n      run: python deploy_cloudformation.py\n\n# Q69 safe error handling: do not fail the pipeline on non-critical errors\n    - name: Check S3 Bucket\n      continue-on-error: true\n      run: python handle_errors.py\n\n# Q70 cleanup EC2: scheduled daily (as written in the source)\non: [schedule: { cron: &#x27;0 0 * * *&#x27; }]\n    - name: Cleanup EC2\n      run: python cleanup_ec2.py</code></pre></div>\n<p>Note: the Q70 <code>on:</code> line is not valid GitHub syntax as written. The correct form is <code>on:</code> then <code>schedule:</code> then <code>- cron: '0 0 * * *'</code>.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0064","card":"q-boto3-018-6-boto3-with-github-actions-q61-70","sec":"boto3-s007","q":"Validate an S3 bucket's contents.","a":"<p>List objects and check for expected files or properties; exit non-zero on failure so the workflow fails.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># validate_s3.py\nimport boto3\nimport sys\n\ndef validate_s3_bucket(bucket_name):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    response = s3_client.list_objects_v2(Bucket=bucket_name)\n    if &#x27;Contents&#x27; not in response:\n        print(&quot;Bucket is empty!&quot;)\n        sys.exit(1)\n    for obj in response[&#x27;Contents&#x27;]:\n        print(f&quot;Found: {obj[&#x27;Key&#x27;]}, Size: {obj[&#x27;Size&#x27;]}&quot;)\n    print(&quot;Validation successful!&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    validate_s3_bucket(&#x27;my-bucket&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0065","card":"q-boto3-019-6-boto3-with-github-actions-q61-70","sec":"boto3-s007","q":"Scale an EKS cluster from a workflow.","a":"<p>The script calls <code>update_nodegroup_config</code> with <code>scalingConfig={'desiredSize': desired_capacity}</code> (same call as Q33), from <code>scale_eks_cluster('my-cluster', 'my-nodegroup', 3)</code>. Workflow uses the <code>workflow_dispatch</code> trigger above.</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0066","card":"q-boto3-019-6-boto3-with-github-actions-q61-70","sec":"boto3-s007","q":"Publish test results to SNS.","a":"<p>Run pytest, then publish a JSON message with a subject.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># publish_sns.py\nimport boto3\nimport json\n\ndef publish_test_results(topic_arn, message):\n    sns_client = boto3.client(&#x27;sns&#x27;)\n    sns_client.publish(\n        TopicArn=topic_arn,\n        Message=json.dumps({&#x27;test_results&#x27;: message}),\n        Subject=&#x27;Test Results&#x27;\n    )\n    print(&quot;Published to SNS&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    publish_test_results(&#x27;arn:aws:sns:us-east-1:123456789012:TestTopic&#x27;, &#x27;Tests passed!&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0067","card":"q-boto3-019-6-boto3-with-github-actions-q61-70","sec":"boto3-s007","q":"Create an S3 bucket and upload artifacts.","a":"<p>Catch <code>BucketAlreadyOwnedByYou</code> to stay idempotent.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># s3_upload.py\nimport boto3\n\ndef create_and_upload(bucket_name, file_path):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    try:\n        s3_client.create_bucket(Bucket=bucket_name)\n        print(f&quot;Created bucket: {bucket_name}&quot;)\n    except s3_client.exceptions.BucketAlreadyOwnedByYou:\n        print(f&quot;Bucket {bucket_name} already exists&quot;)\n    s3_client.upload_file(file_path, bucket_name, file_path)\n    print(f&quot;Uploaded {file_path} to {bucket_name}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    create_and_upload(&#x27;my-unique-bucket-123&#x27;, &#x27;artifact.txt&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0068","card":"q-boto3-019-6-boto3-with-github-actions-q61-70","sec":"boto3-s007","q":"Trigger a CloudFormation deployment.","a":"<p>Create the stack; on <code>AlreadyExistsException</code> fall back to update. Waiters block until completion.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># deploy_cloudformation.py\nimport boto3\n\ndef deploy_stack(stack_name, template_file):\n    cf_client = boto3.client(&#x27;cloudformation&#x27;)\n    with open(template_file, &#x27;r&#x27;) as f:\n        template_body = f.read()\n    try:\n        cf_client.create_stack(\n            StackName=stack_name,\n            TemplateBody=template_body,\n            Capabilities=[&#x27;CAPABILITY_IAM&#x27;]\n        )\n        cf_client.get_waiter(&#x27;stack_create_complete&#x27;).wait(StackName=stack_name)\n        print(f&quot;Stack {stack_name} created&quot;)\n    except cf_client.exceptions.AlreadyExistsException:\n        cf_client.update_stack(\n            StackName=stack_name,\n            TemplateBody=template_body,\n            Capabilities=[&#x27;CAPABILITY_IAM&#x27;]\n        )\n        cf_client.get_waiter(&#x27;stack_update_complete&#x27;).wait(StackName=stack_name)\n        print(f&quot;Stack {stack_name} updated&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    deploy_stack(&#x27;MyStack&#x27;, &#x27;template.yml&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0069","card":"q-boto3-019-6-boto3-with-github-actions-q61-70","sec":"boto3-s007","q":"Handle boto3 errors without breaking the pipeline.","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Catch specific exceptions (<code>ClientError</code>).</li>\n  <li>Log error details.</li>\n  <li>Retry transient errors such as throttling.</li>\n  <li>Use <code>continue-on-error: true</code> for non-critical steps.</li>\n  <li>Exit with proper status codes.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># handle_errors.py\nimport boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\nimport sys\n\ndef safe_s3_operation(bucket_name):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    try:\n        s3_client.head_bucket(Bucket=bucket_name)\n        print(f&quot;Bucket {bucket_name} exists&quot;)\n    except ClientError as e:\n        error_code = e.response[&#x27;Error&#x27;][&#x27;Code&#x27;]\n        if error_code == &#x27;404&#x27;:\n            print(f&quot;Bucket {bucket_name} does not exist&quot;)\n        else:\n            print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\n            sys.exit(1)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    safe_s3_operation(&#x27;my-bucket&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0070","card":"q-boto3-020-6-boto3-with-github-actions-q61-70","sec":"boto3-s007","q":"Clean up unused EC2 instances.","a":"<p>Terminate instances with a given tag older than a threshold (runs on the daily schedule above).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># cleanup_ec2.py\nimport boto3\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n\ndef cleanup_ec2_instances(tag_key, tag_value, max_age_days=7):\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;)\n    response = ec2_client.describe_instances(\n        Filters=[{&#x27;Name&#x27;: f&#x27;tag:{tag_key}&#x27;, &#x27;Values&#x27;: [tag_value]}]\n    )\n    cutoff = datetime.now(timezone.utc) - timedelta(days=max_age_days)\n\n    for reservation in response[&#x27;Reservations&#x27;]:\n        for instance in reservation[&#x27;Instances&#x27;]:\n            launch_time = instance[&#x27;LaunchTime&#x27;]\n            if launch_time &lt; cutoff:\n                instance_id = instance[&#x27;InstanceId&#x27;]\n                ec2_client.terminate_instances(InstanceIds=[instance_id])\n                print(f&quot;Terminated instance: {instance_id}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    cleanup_ec2_instances(&#x27;Environment&#x27;, &#x27;Temp&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0071","card":"q-boto3-021-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"GitHub Actions workflow cannot authenticate with AWS.","a":"<p>Troubleshooting checklist:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Verify <code>AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID</code> and <code>AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY</code> in GitHub Secrets.</li>\n  <li>Check the IAM user/role has the needed permissions.</li>\n  <li>Check the <code>aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials</code> step config.</li>\n  <li>Check the region.</li>\n  <li>Enable debug logging with <code>ACTIONS_STEP_DEBUG: true</code>.</li>\n  <li>Switch to OIDC with an IAM role.</li>\n</ul>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0072","card":"q-boto3-021-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"Timeout listing thousands of S3 objects.","a":"<p>Use a paginator and process in batches to limit memory; add retries for transient errors. (Gotcha: <code>MaxItems</code> caps the total results returned, so it truncates rather than speeds up. Use <code>PageSize</code> to tune per-request size.)</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\n\ndef list_s3_objects(bucket_name):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    paginator = s3_client.get_paginator(&#x27;list_objects_v2&#x27;)\n    try:\n        for page in paginator.paginate(Bucket=bucket_name, PaginationConfig={&#x27;MaxItems&#x27;: 1000}):\n            if &#x27;Contents&#x27; in page:\n                for obj in page[&#x27;Contents&#x27;]:\n                    print(f&quot;Object: {obj[&#x27;Key&#x27;]}&quot;)\n    except ClientError as e:\n        print(f&quot;Error: {e}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    list_s3_objects(&#x27;my-large-bucket&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0073","card":"q-boto3-021-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"Create an EKS cluster with boto3, then configure it with Ansible.","a":"<ol>\n  <li>boto3 creates the cluster and node group and waits for <code>ACTIVE</code>.</li>\n  <li>boto3 reads the cluster details and generates a kubeconfig.</li>\n  <li>Ansible uses the kubeconfig and the <code>k8s</code> module to deploy resources.</li>\n  <li>Run both in a GitHub Actions workflow.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># create_eks.py\nimport boto3\nimport time\n\ndef create_eks_cluster(cluster_name, role_arn, subnets):\n    eks_client = boto3.client(&#x27;eks&#x27;)\n    eks_client.create_cluster(\n        name=cluster_name,\n        roleArn=role_arn,\n        resourcesVpcConfig={&#x27;subnetIds&#x27;: subnets}\n    )\n    while eks_client.describe_cluster(name=cluster_name)[&#x27;cluster&#x27;][&#x27;status&#x27;] != &#x27;ACTIVE&#x27;:\n        print(&quot;Waiting for cluster...&quot;)\n        time.sleep(30)\n    print(&quot;Cluster created&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0074","card":"q-boto3-021-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"\"Rate Exceeded\" when creating many EC2 instances.","a":"<p>Exponential backoff with retries, limit concurrent calls, use batch operations (for example <code>MinCount</code>/<code>MaxCount</code> instead of looping).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\nimport time\n\ndef create_ec2_instances(instance_count):\n    ec2_client = boto3.client(&#x27;ec2&#x27;)\n    for i in range(instance_count):\n        try:\n            ec2_client.run_instances(\n                ImageId=&#x27;ami-12345678&#x27;,\n                InstanceType=&#x27;t2.micro&#x27;,\n                MinCount=1,\n                MaxCount=1\n            )\n            print(f&quot;Created instance {i+1}&quot;)\n        except ClientError as e:\n            if e.response[&#x27;Error&#x27;][&#x27;Code&#x27;] == &#x27;RequestLimitExceeded&#x27;:\n                time.sleep(2 ** i)  # Exponential backoff\n                continue\n            raise e\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    create_ec2_instances(5)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0075","card":"q-boto3-022-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"Detect Terraform drift.","a":"<p>Query AWS, compare with state-file data, report discrepancies (missing resources, modified attributes).</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport json\n\ndef detect_drift(bucket_name):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    try:\n        response = s3_client.head_bucket(Bucket=bucket_name)\n        print(f&quot;Bucket {bucket_name} exists in AWS&quot;)\n        # Compare with Terraform state (assumed to be parsed)\n        terraform_state = {&#x27;versioning&#x27;: &#x27;enabled&#x27;}\n        versioning = s3_client.get_bucket_versioning(Bucket=bucket_name).get(&#x27;Status&#x27;)\n        if versioning != terraform_state[&#x27;versioning&#x27;]:\n            print(f&quot;Drift detected: Versioning is {versioning}, expected {terraform_state[&#x27;versioning&#x27;]}&quot;)\n    except s3_client.exceptions.ClientError:\n        print(f&quot;Bucket {bucket_name} not found in AWS&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    detect_drift(&#x27;my-bucket&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0076","card":"q-boto3-022-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"Credentials exposed in workflow logs.","a":"<ul>\n  <li>Keep credentials in GitHub Secrets.</li>\n  <li>Use OIDC to assume an IAM role instead of long-term keys (workflow below).</li>\n  <li>Mask sensitive values with <code>::add-mask::</code>.</li>\n  <li>Do not log sensitive data in scripts.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">YAML</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># Only the credentials step differs from the Q62 skeleton:\n    - name: Configure AWS Credentials\n      uses: aws-actions/configure-aws-credentials@v2\n      with:\n        role-to-assume: arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/GitHubActionsRole\n        aws-region: us-east-1</code></pre></div>\n<p>(OIDC also needs the job to have <code>permissions: id-token: write</code>.)</p>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0077","card":"q-boto3-022-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"Monitor CloudWatch alarms and trigger an Ansible playbook.","a":"<p>Query alarms, and on <code>ALARM</code> state run <code>ansible-playbook</code> via <code>subprocess</code>. Run on a schedule in GitHub Actions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># monitor_alarms.py\nimport boto3\nimport subprocess\n\ndef monitor_alarms(alarm_name):\n    cw_client = boto3.client(&#x27;cloudwatch&#x27;)\n    response = cw_client.describe_alarms(AlarmNames=[alarm_name])\n    for alarm in response[&#x27;MetricAlarms&#x27;]:\n        if alarm[&#x27;StateValue&#x27;] == &#x27;ALARM&#x27;:\n            print(f&quot;Alarm {alarm_name} triggered!&quot;)\n            subprocess.run([&#x27;ansible-playbook&#x27;, &#x27;remediate.yml&#x27;], check=True)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    monitor_alarms(&#x27;HighCPUAlarm&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0078","card":"q-boto3-023-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"EKS cluster not scaling as expected.","a":"<p>Diagnose:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Check node group config (desired, min, max) with boto3.</li>\n  <li>Check that the Cluster Autoscaler is deployed and configured.</li>\n  <li>Review CloudWatch logs.</li>\n  <li>Validate IAM permissions for scaling.</li>\n  <li>Fix by updating the node group scaling config.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef check_eks_scaling(cluster_name, nodegroup_name):\n    eks_client = boto3.client(&#x27;eks&#x27;)\n    response = eks_client.describe_nodegroup(clusterName=cluster_name, nodegroupName=nodegroup_name)\n    scaling_config = response[&#x27;nodegroup&#x27;][&#x27;scalingConfig&#x27;]\n    print(f&quot;Desired: {scaling_config[&#x27;desiredSize&#x27;]}, Min: {scaling_config[&#x27;minSize&#x27;]}, Max: {scaling_config[&#x27;maxSize&#x27;]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0079","card":"q-boto3-023-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"Automate cleanup of unused S3 buckets.","a":"<p>List buckets, delete those matching a tag or age, schedule in GitHub Actions, and add safeguards (dry run, confirmation). (Gotchas: <code>delete_bucket</code> fails on non-empty buckets, and <code>get_bucket_tagging</code> raises an error for buckets with no tags.)</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code># cleanup_s3.py\nimport boto3\n\ndef cleanup_s3_buckets(tag_key, tag_value):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    response = s3_client.list_buckets()\n    for bucket in response[&#x27;Buckets&#x27;]:\n        tags = s3_client.get_bucket_tagging(Bucket=bucket[&#x27;Name&#x27;]).get(&#x27;TagSet&#x27;, [])\n        if any(tag[&#x27;Key&#x27;] == tag_key and tag[&#x27;Value&#x27;] == tag_value for tag in tags):\n            s3_client.delete_bucket(Bucket=bucket[&#x27;Name&#x27;])\n            print(f&quot;Deleted bucket: {bucket[&#x27;Name&#x27;]}&quot;)\n\nif __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:\n    cleanup_s3_buckets(&#x27;Environment&#x27;, &#x27;Temp&#x27;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0080","card":"q-boto3-023-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"IAM role lacks DynamoDB permissions.","a":"<p>Inspect the <code>AccessDenied</code> error, describe the role's policies with boto3, attach a policy allowing the needed <code>dynamodb:*</code> actions (scope it tighter in practice), rerun.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nfrom botocore.exceptions import ClientError\n\ndef access_dynamodb(table_name):\n    dynamodb = boto3.resource(&#x27;dynamodb&#x27;)\n    try:\n        table = dynamodb.Table(table_name)\n        table.get_item(Key={&#x27;id&#x27;: &#x27;1&#x27;})\n        print(&quot;Access successful&quot;)\n    except ClientError as e:\n        if e.response[&#x27;Error&#x27;][&#x27;Code&#x27;] == &#x27;AccessDeniedException&#x27;:\n            print(&quot;IAM role lacks DynamoDB permissions&quot;)\n        raise e</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0081","card":"q-boto3-024-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"Create with boto3, hand off to Terraform.","a":"<p>Tag resources for identification, generate Terraform config, bring them under management with <code>terraform import</code>, then validate that state matches AWS.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef create_and_tag_s3(bucket_name):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    s3_client.create_bucket(Bucket=bucket_name)\n    s3_client.put_bucket_tagging(\n        Bucket=bucket_name,\n        Tagging={&#x27;TagSet&#x27;: [{&#x27;Key&#x27;: &#x27;ManagedBy&#x27;, &#x27;Value&#x27;: &#x27;Terraform&#x27;}]}\n    )\n    print(f&quot;Created bucket {bucket_name} for Terraform&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0082","card":"q-boto3-024-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"Slow boto3 script in a workflow.","a":"<p>Paginate, cache results to avoid repeat calls, parallelize with <code>ThreadPoolExecutor</code>, use batch APIs.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport boto3\n\ndef list_s3_objects_parallel(bucket_name):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    paginator = s3_client.get_paginator(&#x27;list_objects_v2&#x27;)\n    pages = paginator.paginate(Bucket=bucket_name)\n\n    def process_page(page):\n        return [obj[&#x27;Key&#x27;] for obj in page.get(&#x27;Contents&#x27;, [])]\n\n    with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=4) as executor:\n        results = executor.map(process_page, pages)\n    for keys in results:\n        print(keys)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0083","card":"q-boto3-024-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"Ansible fails because boto3-created resources are not ready yet.","a":"<p>Use boto3 waiters, add retries in the playbook, and run boto3 and Ansible as separate dependent workflow steps.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef create_s3_with_waiter(bucket_name):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    s3_client.create_bucket(Bucket=bucket_name)\n    waiter = s3_client.get_waiter(&#x27;bucket_exists&#x27;)\n    waiter.wait(Bucket=bucket_name)\n    print(f&quot;Bucket {bucket_name} is ready&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0084","card":"q-boto3-024-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"Export EKS logs to S3.","a":"<p>Use CloudWatch Logs <code>create_export_task</code> to an S3 bucket; schedule it in GitHub Actions.</p>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\nimport time\n\ndef export_eks_logs(log_group, bucket_name, prefix):\n    cw_client = boto3.client(&#x27;logs&#x27;)\n    task = cw_client.create_export_task(\n        logGroupName=log_group,\n        fromTime=0,\n        to=int(time.time() * 1000),\n        destination=bucket_name,\n        destinationPrefix=prefix\n    )\n    print(f&quot;Export task created: {task[&#x27;taskId&#x27;]}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false},{"id":"boto3-f0085","card":"q-boto3-025-7-scenario-based-questions-q71-85","sec":"boto3-s008","q":"Script is deleting critical resources.","a":"<p>Safeguards:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Confirmation prompts or dry-run mode.</li>\n  <li>Protect critical resources with tags and filter on them.</li>\n  <li>Restrict IAM to read-only for sensitive resources.</li>\n  <li>Add logging and alerts.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"code-tabs flip-code\"><div class=\"tabbar\"><div class=\"tablist\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Python</button></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"code-copy\" title=\"Copy this code\" aria-label=\"Copy this code\">Copy</button></div><pre><code>import boto3\n\ndef safe_delete_s3(bucket_name, protected_tag=&#x27;Critical&#x27;):\n    s3_client = boto3.client(&#x27;s3&#x27;)\n    tags = s3_client.get_bucket_tagging(Bucket=bucket_name).get(&#x27;TagSet&#x27;, [])\n    if any(tag[&#x27;Key&#x27;] == protected_tag for tag in tags):\n        print(f&quot;Bucket {bucket_name} is protected&quot;)\n        return\n    s3_client.delete_bucket(Bucket=bucket_name)\n    print(f&quot;Deleted bucket: {bucket_name}&quot;)</code></pre></div>","hand":false}];
